The other night an orc within a group of Mordor orcs drank a !oGL and
became and orc-captain, and made me think that some AI-mod ideas could
make monsters that appear in packs -and have some obviously
hierarchical leadership- could be deadlier and harder to deal with
when near a "leader".

These groups could include orcs (with orc-captains); elves, gnomes and
dwarfs with lords and kings, soldiers with sergeants and captains, and
maybe even bees with a queen bee present.

Some ideas might be granting all monsters in the group the same vision
as the leader or even whole group (implying communication of some
kind), lessen the chance of them fleeing, and maybe even increasing to-
hit (assuming some communication about tactics from the leader) or to-
damage (maybe assuming an increase in morale).  You could even go as
far as subordinates trying to heal their leaders, or gaining the
insight to not fire a wand or weapon when one of their group is in the
crossfire.

It would make killing the "leader" a better tactical decision for a
hero.  Aside from beehives and the castle, these groups don't seem to
be generated randomly with leaders, so the patch might also be altered
to have these certain groups sometimes generated with a leader.
(Croesus could be a special case and affect everything generated in
the throne room; likewise any random throne room could do the same if
a "xxx-king" is generated in the room).

The "hive mind" idea could be extended to split puddings, gremlins, or
maybe even among undead when near a lich, or vampires when around a
vampire lord.  Flayers, like liches, don't really appear in packs, so
seem like they should tend not to gain these advantages (they can find
you with telepathy anyway so the bonus vision wouldn't be useful).

Also I've never tried to make a patch before for NH, is there a
"starter" resource for someone trying to do this for the firs time.
I'm going to start easy and try to implement a "Mind Flayer Hall" and
"Lich Lair" before I try anything else much more difficult.



